[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 764,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 701,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119220,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 366,
        "headingId": 701,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Acute undifferentiated leukaemia (AUL) is an acute leukaemia that expresses haematopoietic stem cell markers but no markers that permit lineage assignment.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-01T13:21:24"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 765,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 702,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119221,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 366,
        "headingId": 702,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>9801/3 Acute undifferentiated leukaemia</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-01T13:21:24"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 766,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 703,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119222,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 366,
        "headingId": 703,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>2B33.0 Acute leukaemia, not elsewhere classified</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-01T13:21:24"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 767,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 704,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119223,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 366,
        "headingId": 704,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> stem cell acute leukaemia.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-01T13:21:24"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 768,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 705,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119224,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 366,
        "headingId": 705,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-01T13:21:24"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 769,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 706,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119225,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 366,
        "headingId": 706,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Bone marrow and peripheral blood are always involved.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-01T13:21:24"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 770,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 707,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119226,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 366,
        "headingId": 707,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Patients present with clinical features similar to those of other acute leukaemias, typically secondary to cytopenias {29616841; 31000771; 34540694}.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-01T13:21:24"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 771,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 708,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119227,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 366,
        "headingId": 708,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>The incidence of AUL has decreased over time {31982153}, probably owing to improved classification based on molecular findings and techniques for detecting lineage markers. AUL is estimated to account for 1&ndash;2% of acute leukaemias {29616841; 31982153}; it occurs more commonly in adults, with an M:F&nbsp;ratio of about 1.5:1 {29616841; 30209392; 31817495}.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-01T13:21:24"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 772,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 709,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119228,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 366,
        "headingId": 709,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-01T13:21:24"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 773,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 710,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119229,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 366,
        "headingId": 710,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Approximately 40% of cases have an abnormal karyotype (often a non-complex karyotype). Recurrent mutations include those in <em>PHF6</em>, <em>RUNX1</em>, <em>SRSF2</em>, and <em>ASXL1</em> (each ~40%), and in <em>BCOR</em> (~25%) {29616841; 30209392; 31000771; 34540694}. Gene fusions such as <em>SET</em>::<em>NUP214</em> are also detected in a subset of cases {30209392}. The molecular profile in AUL with <em>RUNX1</em> and <em>ASXL1</em> mutations suggests that AUL may be genetically closer to acute myeloid leukaemia (AML) than to lymphoblastic leukaemia, whereas <em>PHF6</em> mutation supports the notion that AUL may represent a biological continuum of T/myeloid mixed-phenotype acute leukaemia and early T-precursor lymphoblastic leukaemia {30209392; 30530780}.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-01T13:21:24"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 780,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 717,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119230,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 366,
        "headingId": 717,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-01T13:21:24"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 774,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 711,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119231,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 366,
        "headingId": 711,
        "headingText": "<p>Blasts in the blood and bone marrow are usually immature and have no morphological features of differentiation.</p>\r\n\r\n<h5>Immunophenotype</h5>\r\n\r\n<p>Blasts in AUL express no lineage-specific markers and no more than one marker for any given lineage. By definition, they lack cCD3, myeloperoxidase, B-cell markers (e.g. cCD22, CD79a, or strong CD19), and markers of other unusual lineages (including NK&nbsp;cells, megakaryocytes, basophils, or plasmacytoid dendritic cells). Typically, blasts express one myeloid-associated marker (e.g. CD13, CD33, or KIT [CD117]), with two&nbsp;thirds of cases expressing one myeloid marker and one&nbsp;third of cases expressing no myeloid markers. CD34, HLA-DR, and TdT are frequently expressed, whereas CD7 and CD56 are uncommonly expressed {29616841; 31000771; 34540694}.</p>\r\n\r\n<h5>Cytochemistry</h5>\r\n\r\n<p>Blasts are negative for myeloperoxidase and Sudan Black&nbsp;B by definition. Very rarely, blasts may show a positive reaction with nonspecific esterase {31000771}.</p>\r\n\r\n<h5>Differential diagnosis</h5>\r\n\r\n<p>AUL must be distinguished from AML with minimal differentiation in which &ge;&nbsp;2 myeloid-associated markers (e.g. CD13, CD33, and CD117) are expressed. AUL must also be distinguished from, rare mixed-phenotype acute leukaemia (MPAL) subtypes and non-haematopoietic malignancies.</p>\r\n&nbsp;",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-01T13:22:12"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 775,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 712,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119232,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 366,
        "headingId": 712,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>See above.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-01T13:21:24"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 776,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 713,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119233,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 366,
        "headingId": 713,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Cytogenetic analysis and molecular assessment are needed to identify the genetic abnormalities, such as mutations (e.g. <em>PHF6</em>, <em>RUNX1</em>, and <em>SRSF2</em>) and fusion transcripts (e.g. <em>SET</em>::<em>NUP214</em>).</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-01T13:21:24"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 779,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 716,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119234,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 366,
        "headingId": 716,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> &ge;&nbsp;20% blasts in bone marrow and/or blood, lacking expression of immunophenotypic lineage-specific markers; blasts do not express more than one lineage-associated marker of any given lineage; not fulfilling diagnostic criteria for mixed-phenotype acute leukaemia with defined genetic alterations or rare mixed-phenotype acute leukaemia subtypes.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-01T13:21:24"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 777,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 714,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119235,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 366,
        "headingId": 714,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-01T13:21:24"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 778,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 715,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119236,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 366,
        "headingId": 715,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>The clinical management of AUL remains a challenge because of its rarity and lack of therapeutic guidelines. Overall survival has improved with contemporary treatment and differs between paediatric and adult populations {31982153}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-01T13:21:24"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]